WEBVTT

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:36.780
Platform number two: The doors are closing. Please be careful.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.070
Get on! Get on!

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:38.780
Platform number two: The doors are closing. Please be careful.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.490
We made it!

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.410
The bell wasn't for this train?

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.040
Guess we didn't have to run.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.000
Tai...

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:02.760
Platform number six: The doors are closing. Please be careful.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.600
It's leaving this time for sure.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.560
Yeah.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:15.030
Say, won't you have a practice game with us sometime?

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.950
Um, Shinooka... is in Coach Momo's car.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.160
Let's do it.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.120
You!

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.450
This must be some kind of fate.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.410
We'd be delighted to play with you again.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:29.420
All right! Well, our coach's cell phone number is...

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.460
We should agree to it.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.880
Really?

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.880
Next time, let's compete every time.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:43.300
I-I... won't.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.640
Don't say that!

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.600
I-I won't!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.980
But that's... Please!

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.610
Please excuse us!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.030
Excuse me!

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.360
O-Okay.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.860
That's not something you ask for!

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.780
But I... You know...

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.540
Idiot.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.460
At least compete with him during a practice game.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.290
Abe...

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.500
That's the whole reason we're
having a practice game, isn't it?

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.300
Guess I should leave it to Abe, huh?

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:22.010
But even so, we're going to hide our
hand and make them expose everything.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.850
Abe's in a good mood.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.390
So why do you keep saying you won't do it?

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.520
He asked me. I have to answer.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.230
I-I'll end up giving a hit.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.030
Tell me something.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.450
Do you think we walked him because you're no good?

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.740
I wonder what he's asking me.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.160
Is there a deeper meaning behind that?

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.250
Why do you keep gulping like a fish?

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.000
Look, whatever you're thinking right now, just spit it out.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.290
I don't understand.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.500
What? You mean what I'm saying?

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.300
It certainly <i>looks</i> like he's bullying him.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.260
Is that so? I guess you could say that.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.640
Seriously?

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.970
Then, between Sakura and
Tousei's batters, which is scarier?

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.980
They're both scary.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.020
But during the Tousei game, you didn't walk anyone, right?

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.150
You're mixing that up with the shut-out.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:27.490
Even if you were a fastball-throwing pitcher, I would suggest a walk.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.160
Fast... Even Haruna?

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:35.250
Even if it were Haruna or Kanou, I would keep it in mind.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.460
Whether I'd actually use it would depend on the game's flow, but...

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.090
I'm just maintaining a higher probability of winning.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:41.920
Got it?

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.300
I can wait.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.470
Yeah!

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:56.560
I see. I mixed it all up with the shut-out?

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:59.440
No matter who the pitcher is,
a walk would make sense.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:05.400
A-And the shut-out was for my sake.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.080
Do they care for me that much?

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.580
I'll eat a lot,

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.410
and I'll take care of my arm and elbow.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:19.630
I'll work hard so they think highly
of me for as long as possible.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.380
When you get back today, don't do more than play catch.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.050
And no throwing tomorrow.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.970
When I say no throwing, I mean no throwing.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:32.310
After tomorrow, there'll be a bunch of games until the quarter finals.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.680
I talked to the coach as well, and that's what was decided.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:42.110
Not being able to pitch makes me uneasy, but I'm being treated with care.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.490
Resting is also important.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:45.280
Yeah.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.490
Okay.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:49.030
I'll say it again just in case. No throwing at home.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.240
I'm being quite the nag, I must say.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.540
All right! I won't throw!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.580
Somehow, it feels like I'm really getting through.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.000
Should I try talking to him?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.880
About intentional walking...

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.460
I know you don't object to it, but pitchers who do might behave a little differently.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:10.640
I'd say it's just their pride working, but there's no point in walking a batter if the pitcher loses his motivation.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.060
W-Would Haruna lose motivation?

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.350
You really like Haruna.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.520
He has nothing to do with it, does he?

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.270
Plus, it seems like he hates
using his full strength in games.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.400
Then how about Tousei's pitcher?

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.780
Ah, Tousei?

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:31.120
Tousei has no reason to walk Sakitama.
They're picking it up.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.580
If they did, they would probably be seriously flamed...

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.660
by both the opponent and their own team.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:36.410
I see!

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.210
You know, today you had a shut-out with just two safe hits.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.750
A-Abe.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.210
Thank you.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.170
I'm telling you; it's nothing to thank me for.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:54.260
In the seventh inning, I'm sure that Abe tested my strength.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.140
Did I pass?

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.390
That hit was...

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:02.190
Even though I want him to be
confident in himself, it's difficult.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:05.830
For Sakura's at-bat, it was okay for his pitch to get hit, but...

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:08.690
I was, of course, confident that we could catch it.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.280
But...

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:16.990
We were really lucky, being able to pull off something like that in an official game.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:21.210
In the end, Sakura was playing while relying only on his inborn talent.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.120
From here on out,

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.750
will we evade those baseball freaks, who work tirelessly on top of their natural talent,

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:28.630
with this guy alone?

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.090
The conversation ended.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.800
But I was able to say a lot today.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:38.560
When I talk to Abe, I realize a lot of things.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.350
Abe is amazing.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:45.560
If Abe is here, I'll be fine.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:50.360
I guess I'll go to Kawagoe after all.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.490
No, no, no, no, no!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.620
There's no way they'd still be playing by the time I got there. We must have just missed them.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.700
Will the announcement come?

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:00.000
Should be coming soon.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.080
I-It came!

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.000
From who!?

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.380
Mihashi's mom.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:09.550
Th-They did it!

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.840
They did it! They won!

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:12.840
They did!

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.760
Which means...

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.350
We'll get to expose these outfits!

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.060
It's fine, isn't it? I think this much will be okay.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:25.560
That's pretty bad! Don't hide your unfaithfulness!

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:26.940
But I'm kinda anxious about it.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.070
Hey, keep it down!

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.780
The club room isn't for your personal use.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.400
Ochi.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.530
Hi.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.240
It's you guys?

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.240
So those are the outfits?

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.000
They just scream handmade.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.090
What!?

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.010
We make clothes for the dance club too!

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.300
But won't people be able to see under?

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.050
It's surprisingly okay.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:59.930
Also, we're wearing shorts.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.310
Lastly, don't they make your legs look fat somehow?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.940
Maybe because of the high socks?

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:05.850
You think so?

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.900
Ankle socks should be fine.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.020
I think bare legs will look pretty cute.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:11.650
Ochi.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.650
Are you interested in cheering?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:17.990
There's no way I can go out in the sun in an outfit that only covers my torso!

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:18.820
Right.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:19.740
That's true.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:23.750
And anyway, Hamada is gathering people, isn't he?

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:26.710
What? You know Hamada?

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.040
Because he lives alone, you know.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:32.210
If you follow him home, you'll be attacked.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.710
No way!

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.470
But why does he live alone?

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:41.640
Because of company restructuring, aside from Hamada, they're all somewhere in Kyuushuu.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.390
You know a lot, Ochi.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:48.350
All the girls in his class knew.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:51.230
He did part-time jobs to save up for expenses at school and stuff.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.780
He's gone through a lot of hardships, then?

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:58.200
That said, he had a lot of absences
and ended up having to repeat a year.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.660
He seems like an unreliable
guy and I don't really like him.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:05.910
That's why I don't like the fact that you two are involved at all.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:09.210
Just because Yuuri is soft, if you guys neglect the dance club...

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.210
I won't forgive you!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.300
Hey, keep it down.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.170
The club room isn't for your personal use.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.630
Yuuri!

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:17.720
Get off.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.590
Yuuri!

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.680
Oh, cheer girls.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.640
You both look cute.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.640
Yuuri!

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.140
You're so nice!

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.530
18!

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.780
Good. Okay. 19!

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:42.780
Mihashi, look!

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:44.330
Coach Momo!

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.250
Here I go.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.370
Coach! A gift from my mom.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:49.670
Here I go.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.170
You brought them for me?

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.750
I went running and she handed them to me.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.500
Chiyo! Put these in the fridge!

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:55.420
Okay!

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.420
Mihashi, welcome back.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:59.720
Let's take a look at your arm after you wash your face.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:01.470
Does it hurt?

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:02.590
No.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:05.390
Well, your muscles aren't strained. Should be fine.

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:06.930
All right, go stretch a little.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.060
We're borrowing the tennis court at four o'clock.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.100
You're going to rally with Tajima for 30 minutes.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.940
You're being regulated, so take it easy, okay?

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.400
Okay.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:15.980
No throwing.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.480
Tajima.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:18.320
Yes!

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.440
How's your right arm?

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:22.110
I'd say it'll be perfect by tomorrow.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.910
I'm going to the doctor today.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:26.200
Tajima will be completely recovered for the next game.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.830
We're up against Kounan High School in the fourth round.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:28.660
Go rally with Mihashi. The racquets are...

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.750
They came out from the easiest spot in the tournament.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.790
My impression from the video was that they're even weaker than Sakitama.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:34.540
Okay.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.090
For fielding, we'll go back to the original positions. The problem is the batting order.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:41.510
Leaving Tajima as the first batter seems interesting enough,

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:44.680
but we're comparatively weaker with Hanai as fourth batter.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:47.430
If we're talking about hit percentages, then there's Abe to consider, too.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:51.060
But our catcher has his hands
completely full with the pitcher.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:54.270
His load would be too heavy with the fourth batting spot on top of that.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.530
So in the end, we go back to
the order of the Tousei match?

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:02.110
Hey, is Oki practicing his curveball?

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:03.780
Maybe.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.660
It's so nice to be left-handed.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:09.490
If I were left-handed, I would have been a pitcher.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:13.330
You want to be a pitcher?

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.920
No, hitting is my priority.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.130
If I were a pitcher, my number of at-bats would decrease.

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:23.340
If you were serious about it, I wouldn't stand a chance.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.840
Then how about Hanai?

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.180
Then what about Oki?

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:32.310
You wouldn't stance a chance against those two either?

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:37.150
A-As long as Abe is here, I won't lose.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.150
So you'll lose if Abe isn't here?

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:43.900
Abe... is always here.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.740
Always?

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:51.450
Tajima, Mihashi, it's almost four.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.660
Okay.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.620
Butt stretch!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:02.630
Abe will always be here.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:05.800
For three years, he won't get injured or sick.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:12.770
There aren't any other reasons he would be gone... are there?

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.520
One, two, one, two.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.440
Let's go!

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.520
One, two, one, two.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:19.310
Let's go!

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:20.980
One, two, one, two.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:21.690
Takii's still running?

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:22.860
Let's go!

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:23.820
One, two, one, two.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.240
Isn't he exercising more than when he was manager?

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:26.070
Let's go!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.240
One, two, one, two.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.240
Coach, I'm heading back!

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.070
Let's go!

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:29.700
One, two, one, two.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.280
Coach, what's for dinner?

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:32.450
Let's go!

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.790
Gudaku's piping hot miso ramen!
One, two, one, two.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.250
Let's go!

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.290
One, two, one, two.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.170
Ramen!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:43.210
One, two, one, two.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:44.130
Ramen!

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:46.340
One, two, one, two.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:46.470
Idiots.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.800
Ramen!

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:55.680
Hey. What's your weight today?

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.520
Good morning.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:00.690
It's 53 kilos today.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:02.900
You've regained most of your weight. Good job.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:05.610
I was praised first thing in the morning.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:08.740
Tajima! Is today's practice still adjusted for your injury?

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.240
I've got normal practice starting today!

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:13.450
Mihashi. Tajima's gone back to a regular training menu.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.790
You'll stretch and play catch with me.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:17.540
All of it?

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.330
I know you usually do your stretching with Tajima,

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:23.590
but there's something weird and scary about it.

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:27.510
Including catch, I'll be watching the number of pitches you throw.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.510
Our schedule is really packed,

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:34.720
so don't catch a cold from the air
conditioner or eat anything weird.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:39.020
Oh yeah. The sports festival events were decided, right?

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.650
You didn't sign up for anything strange, did you?

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:42.440
Abe's so annoying.
I asked Hamada...

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:43.860
What a nag.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:44.650
I don't want to be a pitcher after all.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.110
I'm in the cavalry battle.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.400
Lose the cavalry battle immediately.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:50.860
I'm being treated importantly.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.910
Abe... Th-Thank you!

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:55.830
Yeah.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:59.460
A-Abe...

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:03.380
Will you... quit being catcher?

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.340
Like that would happen, you misguided fool!

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:08.550
What part of me gave you that impression!?

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:09.920
You're going to make me cry in the end!

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:13.640
Shit. In any case, the game is our priority right now.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:16.140
The higher we rise, the larger the pitcher's role becomes.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:20.100
I want to at least get him into top shape.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:24.060
I won't yell anymore, so come out.

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:25.900
Let's go.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:36.120
If Abe won't quit being catcher, then I can be the ace.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:42.670
Abe will catch the ace's pitches.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.840
My feet won't move.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.920
I feel like I'm underwater.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.430
I won't be able to react to a hit like this.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.390
Tied in the bottom of the ninth inning?

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:58.470
This is bad... I'm begging you.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.310
Don't hit it over here!

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.980
Wake up already!

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:13.030
I woke you up because you were having a nightmare.

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:16.780
Waking up with someone in your face, you'd be surprised too.

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:19.700
You use judo on people when you're surprised?

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:23.580
Shut up. Any changes to the starting lineup?

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.540
Nope. There shouldn't be any problems.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:26.670
About Takeshi...

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.550
He's gotten taller.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:33.220
After entering this tournament, it's like he's come into his own.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:35.590
He never used to have a lot of guts.

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:38.430
But I was sold on his skill and straightforward honesty.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.680
You really pushed for him, didn't you?

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:41.720
You've got a good eye.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:45.850
I'm praising you.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:49.270
Well, that's probably because he's worked hard.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:53.150
I see. Kids are amazing.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:56.450
It's impossible to think that I was among them just two years ago.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:59.740
Are you going senile already? I'm going ahead.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:03.040
Hey! I was talking about something good, too.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.250
For breakfast, I have to peel 100 potatoes.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.040
Thanks for the hard work.

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:12.090
It's already just a memory for you?

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.090
I'm envious.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.880
Hey.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:18.930
Takeshi.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:19.930
Morning...

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.810
You're going to be a starting member today too.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:27.150
Although it seemed like the coach was wavering,

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.900
I pushed hard.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:31.070
Th-Thank you very much!

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:33.400
I think it'd be fine for you to play normally today.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:36.450
But don't forget your role.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:39.160
Yes!

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.450
Be sure to stay close!

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.000
A lot of people will be coming.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.120
Okay!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.920
We're going to the stands near third base.

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:52.550
This place is different from the
opening ceremony, but is it okay?

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.840
Even tough it's in Oomiya, this stadium is operated by the city.

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:00.340
The opening ceremony was held in a baseball stadium managed by the prefecture.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:01.510
It's just next door.

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:04.850
If we win today, we'll be able to play there next.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.810
Somehow, Hanai seems happy about the other stadium.

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.190
B-Because it's big?

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:13.400
Big? Are you talking about the prefecture's management?

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.320
The prefectural management is more widespread on both sides...

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.780
but the center is the same as here.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:19.860
He misunderstood.

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.490
If it's not because it's big, then...

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.580
B-Because of the opening ceremony?

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:28.000
The opening ceremony is held there every year.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:33.500
And the games that are managed by the prefecture are decided from the outset.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:37.050
Also, you probably don't know since you were in Gunma, but...

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:42.010
in Saitama, the local broadcast station airs all games managed by the prefecture on TV.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:42.760
TV?

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.510
They're back on track!

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:49.020
My parents told me to win today, no matter what.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:50.730
Give me a break, huh?

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:55.270
All right. Work hard and stick with us.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:58.900
Look, Mrs. Suyama, the kids are coming!

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:01.860
I see them. They did say they were coming to watch the game.

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:06.660
If only they could hold all baseball games in the same stadium.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.870
Plus, the next game will finally be on TV.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:10.920
I wonder if someone will get filmed?

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.790
Maybe I'll come all dressed up.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:17.340
Hey, wait, Mrs. Hanai! When I was talking about someone getting filmed, I meant the boys.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:19.220
No way! Jeez!

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:22.640
Hey...

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.890
If they win today...

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:29.350
they'll be in Saitama's best 16.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:32.520
Shinooka. Are there any changes in the starting lineup?

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:34.900
There aren't any changes for either school.

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:38.360
And in every game, Bijou uses two or three relief pitchers.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.740
Relief pitchers? And three of them?

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:47.660
Even though there are three of them, I think it's a last resort to make up for not gathering pitchers.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:48.790
What do you mean?

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.870
Bijou changed coaches two years ago, right?

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:55.000
It seems like the replacement was a student and it created a stir.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.710
Our upperclassmen avoided the school.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.340
No one from my school has gone to Bijou for the past three years too.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:05.600
Now that you mention it, Bijou has a strong image, but I don't think I saw them last summer.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.930
Um...

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.180
Last year, they were eliminated in the first round.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:12.730
In the fall, they won one game and lost in the first round of the prefectural tournament.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:16.900
But in the spring, they got into the best 16 and are the D seed in this tournament.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.360
She sure is fast.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:21.030
Then our coach is more amazing.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.610
We made it to the fourth round in our first year.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:25.740
Well, that's if you only look at this tournament.

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:30.700
But to work out using three pitchers is pretty tough.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:33.750
Being able to do that when you're around twenty years old is pretty impressive.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.540
Twenty?

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:36.960
Twenty, huh...

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.290
Second year in college?

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.090
So then...

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.550
How old are you, coach?

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:47.300
Twenty-three.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.430
Twenty-three. That's... three
years older than my brother?

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.480
Six? No, seven years older?

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:54.850
That's awkward. Awkward!?

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:57.440
There's no need to be
thinking about that anyway!

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.230
Number 8 is the catcher, Kurata?

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:04.780
He's hit a lot in this tournament.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.410
The other batters we need to watch out for are number 4, Wada...

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:10.910
and the one who wasn't picked as catcher and became right fielder, Miyata.

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:11.950
My older brother's wife is 23.

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:13.330
Since we've come all this way to watch,
I should point out some things to Mihashi.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:15.210
She's pregnant, so her boobs are pretty big.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:15.870
Mi...

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:17.750
Will you... quit being catcher?

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:23.210
He looks nice and relaxed, so I'll leave it to Tajima.

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.930
Yeah. Yeah, okay.

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:29.430
Was that Kaji on the phone?

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:30.760
Oh, Hamada.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:32.720
How's it going inside?

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:34.060
Seems like it's over.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:36.020
Bijou's seven-inning shut-out.

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:37.730
All right!

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:39.730
You guys ready? Huh?

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.690
J-Just a second.

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:45.690
Let's take them off already. The game's going to start.

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:48.820
Y-You're right. It's really hot anyway.

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.200
Okay, here we go.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:51.330
Yeah.

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.120
There! We're ready!

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:55.580
Ready!

00:21:57.620 --> 00:22:00.420
Your socks got shorter.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:01.670
Then, shall we?

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:04.090
He doesn't seem...

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:05.880
...dangerous at all.

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:07.840
Play ball!

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:46.440
The Nishiura baseball team is advancing smoothly.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:51.700
Starting from the fourth round, cheer girls are joining in too, and the stands are very lively.

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:56.280
But in those stands is Bijoudai Sayama High School's baseball team.

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:59.620
It seems like they're there to watch their next opponents.

00:23:59.620 --> 00:24:05.330
But supervisor Takii and coach Roka seem to be grinning fearlessly about something.

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:07.170
Next time:

00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:08.630
Slow Changes.

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:10.670
We use our tools with care.
